[10.076413, "o", "\r\n"]
[10.838769, "o", "\r\n=== agentmachi: hub 'myproject' ===\r\naddress: ws://localhost:8766\r\ntokens:  /tmp/tmp.FiNd3Tv8gj/home/.agentmachi/myproject/tokens.json  (0600 — do not commit!)\r\nrules:   /tmp/tmp.FiNd3Tv8gj/home/.agentmachi/myproject/data/rules.md\r\ndata:    /tmp/tmp.FiNd3Tv8gj/home/.agentmachi/myproject/data\r\n"]
[10.839853, "o", "\r\nidentities (config):\r\n  human  human  [-]\r\n\r\nhuman (TUI):\r\n  agentmachi tui --name myproject\r\n\r\nagent joins (listen + send; paste one of these to an agent):\r\n  AGENTMACHI_HUB=myproject CHAT_URL=ws://localhost:8766 CHAT_NICK=agent1 agentmachi listen\r\n  AGENTMACHI_HUB=myproject CHAT_URL=ws://localhost:8766 agentmachi send \"@agent1 hi\" --as agent2\r\n  on loopback and inside a tailnet no token is needed — the hub hands out a\r\n  free nick itself. For a public bind (0.0.0.0) or a machine outside the\r\n  tailnet add an entry to tokens.json first and pass CHAT_TOKEN=<that token>\r\n\r\nsentence for an agent (join skill):\r\n  \"join agentmachi 'myproject' (ws://localhost:8766) as agent1\"\r\n\r\nroom runs in the background (PID 385042), log: /tmp/tmp.FiNd3Tv8gj/home/.agentmachi/myproject/serve.log\r\n  who IS on the channel:  agentmachi tui --name myproject\r\n  which rooms exist:      agentmachi list\r\n  stop it:                agentmachi stop --name myproject\r\n"]
